name issue_133_pacer_v2_outage_8s
describe Video-only call, 8 s outage at 10 s: video must come back after link-up (issue #133)
# Before the fix the outage monitor paused the encoder, nothing was sent, no feedback came back and the
# video never resumed (frames_rendered 300, one 30 s pause). libwebrtc keeps the link alive with
# PacingController::ShouldSendKeepalive: a padding packet every 500 ms while the pacer is paused.
# With the fix video resumes ~0.3 s after link-up (seed 1: 8 s outage -> pause/freeze about 8.3 s).
seed 1
duration 40s
audio off
at 0s capacity=3000kbps delay=40ms queue=300ms
at 10s down
at 18s up
expect video.frames_rendered > 850
# PR #328 (link_headroom, refs #326; program.md 0.2, Owner sign-off 2026-10-23): was < 9500. Ours 9809 on seed 1;
# libwebrtc per seed 9825/10002/9788/9756/9766/9428/9742/9783/9766/9807 on #328's compare-webrtc (worst 10002).
# PR #336 (session started before the first frame, refs #331; program.md 0.2, needs-human): was < 9810. Ours 9817 on seed 1;
# libwebrtc per seed 9825/9798/9780/9952/9773/9791/9404/10061/9769/9759 on main's compare-webrtc after #340 (seed 1 9825).
# Issue #355 (rate_utilization_tracker on by default, as libwebrtc; program.md 0.2, needs-human): was < 9820. Ours 9952
# on seed 1 (seeds 1-10 mean 9864; 9900 without); libwebrtc's seed 1 is 9825 and its worst 10061, as above.
# After #361 (XR RTT) merged in (program.md 0.2; accepted by the Owner on 2026-10-24): was < 10000. Seeds 1-10 with the tracker 10198/9387/10120/
# 9434/10117/10211/9399/9874/9794/9827 (mean 9836), without 9439/9743/10052/9846/9781/10147/9763/10008/9952/9819 (mean
# 9855); libwebrtc mean 9791, worst 10061. Seed 1 is past libwebrtc's worst seed.
expect video.pause_total_ms < 10250
